                "text": "I'm noticing each shape's impurity cells (8s) get replaced with the shape's own color, effectively cleaning them, and then the cleaned shapes get repositioned to new locations in the output grid.\n\nThe direction of movement seems tied to where the 8-impurity sits within each shape: the 6's 8 was at its top-right corner and it moved up-right, the 4's 8 was at its top-left corner and it moved up-left, and the 3's 8 was at its bottom-right corner and it moved down-right. So the rule appears to be that each shape shifts one step diagonally toward the corner where its impurity marker was located. I feel confident enough in this pattern to test it.",
